From 5c60af8c2dc28016d036786d7d22854c48784a9f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Golle <daniel@makrotopia.org>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 20:40:43 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] waylandhost: serve kodi_web_v1

Bind the manager global, keep one view object per profile with its
surface, and turn the client's requests into observer callbacks and
the observer's commands into events on the host thread. A file handed
to a view is sent and closed by the host. A favicon buffer is logged
with its profile and size and released.

Input goes to the active view, as set_active defines it: activating
a view moves the keyboard focus to its surface, deactivating it takes
the focus away, and a view surface coming up takes the focus only
while its view is active, so a view kept running in the background
cannot hold the input of the one being shown.

Signed-off-by: Daniel Golle <daniel@makrotopia.org>
---
 .../linux/waylandhost/WaylandHost.cpp         | 344 +++++++++++++++++-
 xbmc/platform/linux/waylandhost/WaylandHost.h |  74 ++++
 2 files changed, 417 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

